---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import CsvToJson from '../../components/CsvToJson.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="CSV to JSON Converter" description="Convert CSV data into a clean JSON array, handling quoted fields correctly.">
  <CsvToJson client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>Handles quoted fields</h2>
  <p>Unlike a naive comma-split, this parser correctly handles quoted values containing commas — common in exported spreadsheet data.</p>

  <h2>Common CSV to JSON Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Using a naive comma-split</strong> instead of a proper CSV parser, breaking on any field that legitimately contains a comma within quotes.</li>
    <li><strong>Not checking for inconsistent column counts</strong> across rows, which can indicate a malformed source CSV.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This CSV to JSON Converter</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Converting a spreadsheet export into JSON for use in an application</li>
    <li>Preparing CSV data for import into a JSON-based API or database</li>
    <li>Quickly inspecting CSV data in a more structured JSON format</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
